========================================================================
0c) StackGen discovery-modules repositories
========================================================================

When `repository_full_name` ∈ {${discovery_repositories_list}}:

  1. Persist note `discovery_repo=true` as soon as the repo matches (`check-info-and-clone` step 1).
%{ if discovery_issue_label != "" ~}
  2. **Label gate first** (`check-info-and-clone` step 2 — discovery layout SOP §1): check `issue_labels` from the webhook payload before any other work. On failure, Template E (GitHub path) and STOP.
  3. Only after `gate_result` is `pass` or `pass_legacy_label`: load skill `${sop_discovery_layout_name}` before module resolution or greenfield scaffold.
%{ else ~}
  2. Load skill `${sop_discovery_layout_name}` BEFORE module resolution or greenfield scaffold. It overrides generic `modules/` layout rules.
%{ endif ~}
  4. In `implement-module`, use discovery layout SOP §2 for existence checks under `aws/`, `gcp/`, `azurerm/` — never `modules/` or `terraform/modules/`.
  5. In `implement-module`, when `not_found` + greenfield: spawn **Template I** (`implement-module-discovery-scaffold`) per discovery layout SOP §4 — **do NOT** spawn Template H (registry wrap) on these repos.
  6. Approved subagent name for this stage additionally includes: `implement-module-discovery-scaffold`.
  7. **Forbidden in `check-info-and-clone`** before the label gate passes: `graph_query`, `load_skill` (including this layout SOP), `check-info-and-clone-fetch` when title/body/labels are already in the webhook payload.

========================================================================
2a-discovery) Resolution override (discovery repos only)
========================================================================

After generic §2a steps (a)–(d), if `discovery_repo=true`, re-run existence per `${sop_discovery_layout_name}` §2 and let that SOP's result supersede `module_paths` / `module_resolution_confidence` when the discovery algorithm is more specific.
